WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.024
(audience applause)

00:00:01.024 --> 00:00:05.030
- [Kelly] So I already
introduced you to Deon,

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.290
but I have to tell you that -

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:07.730
I know I wrote you this card backstage,

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.800
I don't know if you've read it yet -

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.520
but you, randomly, I don't think you know,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.130
but you met my friend, Brynn Cartelli.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.210
- [Cody] Yes!
- She was my Voice winner,

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.270
my first season on The
Voice and her mama, Deb.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.600
And they were in New York city

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.310
and here's the test of a true kind person.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.970
He didn't know them, like
whatever, but you took time

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:25.540
and you took a photo, its so,

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.507
it's so sweet!
(audience applause)

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:30.430
That's Brynn's mama, Deb,
and they're my friends

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.049
and they said you were so kind to them.

00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:33.120
- They were so sweet, I remember.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.040
My boyfriend lives like
right around the corner.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.350
So we were just having dinner
and they were so sweet and-

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.840
- They were very excited and you were-

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.650
And I know that it sucks sometimes
when you're out to dinner

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.510
and you're like, I just want
to like live my life sometimes.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.270
And it was just, but
it was very kind, like,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.590
not everybody's that kind, so anyway,

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:47.629
I just want to say thank
you saying and being nice.

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:48.830
- Of course! It comes
with the territory, okay?

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:49.663
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:51.870
Well what do you, do you like working out?

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:52.760
Do you Peloton?

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.715
Do you do anything like that?

00:00:53.715 --> 00:00:54.548
- You said what?

00:00:54.548 --> 00:00:57.300
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.150
- [Kelly] Nope.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.584
- Peloton?
(laughter)

00:00:59.584 --> 00:01:01.440
- Do you work out at
all? How do you work out?

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.341
Do you work out?

00:01:02.341 --> 00:01:04.459
- Uh, yeah...

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:06.376
(audience laughter)
- And how so?

00:01:06.376 --> 00:01:08.507
- I think you probably work
out as much as I do then.

00:01:08.507 --> 00:01:10.220
(laughing)
- Yeah.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.696
Carrying laundry to the laundry room.

00:01:12.696 --> 00:01:13.730
(audience laughing)
- Hey, five minutes

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:14.670
with a towel.
- I just love it

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.320
cause my house is being
renovated right now.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.000
So I'm like, oh, I can't, cause it's like,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.450
everything's so messed up
right now so I can't work out.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.200
It's like my, I will find an excuse.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.330
But like Deon, you went through a lot

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.790
to get where you are today, right?

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:29.720
- Absolutely, you know,
growing up in Greensboro,

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:31.270
North Carolina it was
like, it was challenging.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.340
My mom was a single parent.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.100
She worked a lot of like blue collar jobs,

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.320
as a waitress, she worked at the Coliseum.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.770
So, it was really
challenging growing up and

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.780
I'm always like, I look
back at that adversity

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.707
and I look at the things
that I went through.

00:01:45.707 --> 00:01:46.540
- Mm.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:48.360
- And I look at where, where I came from.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.810
Like at a point we were homeless.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.973
Like we were living in motels
or I was staying with parents,

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.380
parents of my friends.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.213
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:56.213 --> 00:01:58.150
- And you look back and you're like, wow.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:01.360
That was a time that I was
really going through it.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.010
But it always gave me that drive.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.780
It always gave me that push that I knew

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:08.001
I never wanted to be in that place again.

00:02:08.001 --> 00:02:09.110
(audience applause)
- I think that's how you

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.120
build such an amazing work ethic as well.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.980
Because we, our family
was similar, like me,

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.280
my mom was single for
a good part of my life

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.760
when I was a kid and
so it made me watch her

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.593
work so hard.
- Yeah.

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:20.410
- And she was trying to
overcome so much and like,

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.700
it made me work really
hard and I really like,

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.180
that's why everybody's always
like, you have so many jobs!

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.297
I'm like, y'all, my
mom had all these jobs.

00:02:25.297 --> 00:02:26.985
But everybody's got a lot of jobs, right?

00:02:26.985 --> 00:02:28.303
(audience applause)
- Everybody got a lot of jobs!

00:02:28.303 --> 00:02:30.890
- Everybody's trying to
hustle and make it happen.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:33.010
But I think that it does
help you, don't you agree?

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.404
Like how you grow up, it
really just kind of molds you.

00:02:35.404 --> 00:02:36.343
- Absolutely, yeah.

00:02:36.343 --> 00:02:40.500
Because your path dictates
who you become, you know?

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.333
- [Cody] Absolutely.

00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:44.078
- And then once you do
get it, you cherish it

00:02:44.078 --> 00:02:48.286
in a way that other people
who was just given it to-

00:02:48.286 --> 00:02:49.119
(audience applause)

00:02:49.119 --> 00:02:50.720
- You almost feel sorry for them,

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:51.940
because they don't know the difference.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.773
They don't.

00:02:52.773 --> 00:02:53.606
And they don't even
appreciate it, it's just you-

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.439
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:54.439 --> 00:02:55.571
- Absolutely do.

00:02:55.571 --> 00:02:58.194
So you met one of your
idols recently, right?

00:02:58.194 --> 00:02:59.027
- [Cody] Yes.

00:02:59.027 --> 00:03:00.330
- Working? So wait, how
was it and who was it?

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.163
Tell everybody.

00:03:01.163 --> 00:03:03.674
- Oh, so Mel C! Sporty Spice!

00:03:03.674 --> 00:03:05.744
(audience cheering)

00:03:05.744 --> 00:03:07.778
- Was (sighs) an icon.

00:03:07.778 --> 00:03:09.200
- [Kelly] Still looks fantastic!

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.033
- [Cody] Amazing!

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.030
- [Kelly] Oh my god!

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.550
- She is the hardest working
member of the Spice Girls.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.820
So, you know, like, and it still shows,

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.840
it was just surreal

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.230
having this person I looked
up to and being on the

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.120
same show as her.
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.550
- And honestly, I loved sharing
this experience with her

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.900
because it's really, you've
done reality TV shows.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:28.733
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:28.733 --> 00:03:30.150
- Like, it's nerve wracking.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.030
You don't know what's going to happen

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.420
at the end of every episode.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.253
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:34.253 --> 00:03:36.380
- And so, what I loved
about having her by my side

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.040
was always talking about
like the nervousness

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.460
and the anxiety that we might
feel before we performed.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:43.610
And I was like, if a Spice
Girl who sold out stadiums

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.270
is getting nervous, like
it's okay that I'm nervous,

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:47.470
you know.
- But everyone I talked to

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.930
that does these shows they always say,

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.480
it's just like the hardest thing ever.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.313
Everyone.
- [Cody] It is grueling.

00:03:51.313 --> 00:03:53.510
- It doesn't if matter
if it's like an Olympian

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:55.330
or a housewife, it
doesn't matter who it is.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.770
They're all like, it's the
hardest thing ever schedule wise.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.603
- [Cody] It is. It is crazy. Its like-

00:03:58.603 --> 00:03:59.979
- Why did you sign up to do it?

00:03:59.979 --> 00:04:00.900
That's my-
(audience laughs)

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.490
Like as soon as someone
says that I'm like, never,

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:05.620
I'm like nope.
(audience laughs)

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.440
- I hid, I hid that I liked their song.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.273
- [Cody] Yeah?

00:04:10.273 --> 00:04:11.940
- I hid that I liked that song.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:12.793
- Oh, it was like a guilty pleasure?

00:04:12.793 --> 00:04:14.330
- When it first came out.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:15.838
- Oh yeah. What do you mean?
- I wouldn't let nobody know

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:16.671
that I loved it.
- If You Wanna Be My Lover?

00:04:16.671 --> 00:04:17.504
- But you were turning it up.

00:04:17.504 --> 00:04:18.337
You were turning up

00:04:18.337 --> 00:04:19.170
Wannabe in the car.
- Yeah like my boys

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.360
would get in the car and I
be like, all right y'all,

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.401
I'll talk to y'all later.

00:04:22.401 --> 00:04:24.861
♪ And I' ll tell you what
what I really really want ♪

00:04:24.861 --> 00:04:27.861
(audience applause)

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.785
- Oh my god, I love it!
It reached everyone.

00:04:32.785 --> 00:04:33.618
- [Cody] Everybody!

00:04:33.618 --> 00:04:34.451
- It reached everyone.

00:04:34.451 --> 00:04:37.290
Well, you had a Grease theme, so,

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.123
and there was a week on
Dancing With The Stars

00:04:38.123 --> 00:04:38.960
where we did a Grease theme.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.021
But actually that wasn't
your first time playing

00:04:41.021 --> 00:04:41.854
a greaser.
- It was not.

00:04:41.854 --> 00:04:43.063
- I think we have a clip.

00:04:43.063 --> 00:04:44.852
- [Cody] Ahh, I knew this
was where this was going!

00:04:44.852 --> 00:04:47.843
♪ Go grease lightning you're
burning up the quarter mile ♪

00:04:47.843 --> 00:04:50.453
♪ Grease lighting, go grease lighting ♪

00:04:50.453 --> 00:04:51.718
♪ Go grease lightning ♪

00:04:51.718 --> 00:04:53.761
♪ You're coasting through
the heat lap trials ♪

00:04:53.761 --> 00:04:56.221
♪ Grease lightning, go grease lightning ♪

00:04:56.221 --> 00:04:57.270
(audience applause)
- Here's the thing.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.410
I was a total choir kid too.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.247
I did that move as well.

00:05:01.247 --> 00:05:02.620
- Did you?
- I did that same thing.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.970
I didn't look as cool, but I
didn't have a leather jacket.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.881
I look like a hot mess, then too.

00:05:06.881 --> 00:05:08.400
(Kelly laughing)
- Wow.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.570
I mean, look at that hairstyle

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.077
and that very heteronormative
jean, you know like-

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:13.570
(everyone laughing)

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:16.014
It was, I wasn't in my groove just yet.

00:05:16.014 --> 00:05:16.847
- Yeah.

